From f00c6733aa4405556320b8b10ba1c693fc118f91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Evolution BR811 <344454957+Evolution-BR811@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:35:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] BR1611: OPN-style WMS, waves inside each operator

The WMS now works like the OPN (YM2612): 8 algorithms and feedback,
operator AM with the LFO's tremolo (AMS), OPN detune, operator mask, and
the same instrument editor (FM tab and FM/OP macros) and effects as the
OPN. Each operator still plays its own waveform, which now lives in the
instrument: a wave button next to every operator opens an editor to
draw it, pick a preset (the OPL3 waves among them), type values in
decimal or hex, copy it from another operator or a wavetable, and load
or save .fuw files.

Instruments from before this change load with sine waves.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KMJUrc1fn7dir5w2PfSPK2
